My whole life my mother and others told me this lie about rich people "writing things off" and "not paying taxes". It was a fallacy. I own two businesses. In order to write something off, then you must pay for something. The write off is never larger nor as large as the original expense. 

Example: Car lease for a Real Estate Agent could be $500/ month. You can't write off $500 a month for a whole year. Your wire off is only a percentage of use for business. Peoole told me my whole life business owners get to write off their car payments totally because of a sign or wrap on the vehicle. No they don't. As a self-employed real estate agent, how much you can write off depends strictly on your business-use percentage of the vehicle. The IRS does not allow a 100% write-off for a leased vehicle unless it is used 100% exclusively for business, with zero personal or commuting miles. Driving my car from my house to the office is commuting. Driving my car from my house to a listing is commuting. I can't write any of that off. Only about 50-70% if you are really successful. You are just getting a break but you already spent that $500. It isn't free money. You can research it yourself. Elon simply postponed the taxes a few years. He paid a huge penalty for doing it. Higher tax bracket. 37% plus state of California which is insanely high.

