Take this on a more personal basis for an average person. Let's say you buy a house. You live in that house your entire life. You bought it for $100,000 and it's now worth a million dollars. But you never paid taxes on that $900,000 that increased your net worth. You will pay that when you sell your house. Although there are also some tax laws aspects where sometimes you may not have to pay taxes on some or all of it depending on what the money is being used for. If we decided to tax you say 15% on that $900,000 then most people could only pay that by selling their house or taking a loan out. It's the same with Elon Musk because he could only pay it by selling some of his company. And if the value of the company dropped then what are you going to do, refund the money he paid in those taxes?

